Size the activity bar overflow from the height an item is drawn at.

VSCodroid raises .activitybar .action-item to 44px for a finger pointer (the touch
stylesheet MainActivity injects). The overflow is sized from compositeSize, which up to
1.133 was the constant 52, above that floor, so the bar always had room. In 1.139.1 it
is the height the workbench draws an item at itself: 28px for the compact bar. By that
count every view fits, so on a phone in landscape no "..." menu appears while the drawn
bar is taller than its room, and the Accounts and Manage buttons are pushed below it,
out of reach.

An item is now sized at the floor whenever the pointer is coarse, the media query the
stylesheet uses, so the two cannot disagree. The number lives in TOUCH_ACTION_HEIGHT,
and ActivityBarItemSizeTest compares it with the stylesheet's.

0008 measures the room the bar has; this measures what an item takes of it.

